# Line endings: normalized to LF in the repository and on checkout.
#
# Windows tooling on this machine rewrites files with CRLF, which produced
# whole-file phantom diffs on LICENSE, .gitignore, styles.scss, README.md,
# index.qmd, every projects/*.qmd, the publish workflow and the tech stack
# SVG — hundreds of lines of noise that buried the real change in every diff
# and had to be classified by hand before each commit.
#
# Every blob in HEAD is already LF, so this is a policy declaration and not a
# rewrite: git normalizes on the way into the index, and the phantom diffs
# stop appearing. No renormalization commit is needed.
#
# LF rather than CRLF because the site renders and deploys on ubuntu runners,
# and because a CNAME carrying a trailing CR silently breaks custom-domain
# parsing on GitHub Pages — the failure mode is a site that quietly falls back
# to the github.io address.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never examined for line endings, never normalized.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.db   binary
*.sqlite binary
